       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** Metformin's maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (usually 850 mg three times daily). For extended-release it's 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** The order is about twice the maximum. That raises the risk of severe GI effects and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total per day, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily, or another dose\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that. I'd suggest adding a note with the clinical rationale."
